          <!-- ViT for Urban Change Detection -->
          <article class="project-card fade-in tilt-card" aria-label="Vision Transformer for Urban Change Detection project">
            <div class="card-header">
              <h4 class="card-title">Vision Transformer for Urban Change Detection</h4>
              <span class="status-badge status-active">Active</span>
            </div>
            <p class="card-period">Jan 2025 &ndash; Present</p>
            <div class="stack-tags">
              <span class="stack-tag">PyTorch</span>
              <span class="stack-tag">Albumentations</span>
              <span class="stack-tag">TensorBoard</span>
              <span class="stack-tag">LEVIR-CD</span>
            </div>
            <p class="card-description">Implemented a Vision Transformer from scratch in PyTorch for bi-temporal change detection using Sentinel-2 satellite imagery. Built patch embedding, positional encoding, multi-head self-attention, and transformer encoder blocks without pretrained modules. Built a Siamese encoder architecture with a segmentation decoder for urban growth detection. Produced segmentation change maps and evaluated performance using IoU, F1, Dice, precision, and recall against CNN baselines.</p>
            <table class="results-table" aria-label="Model performance comparison">
              <thead>
                <tr>
                  <th>Model</th>
                  <th>F1</th>
                  <th>IoU</th>
                </tr>
              </thead>
              <tbody>
                <tr>
                  <td>U-Net</td>
                  <td>0.8843</td>
                  <td>0.7927</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td>Swin</td>
                  <td>0.8613</td>
                  <td>0.7564</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td>ViT</td>
                  <td>0.8236</td>
                  <td>0.7001</td>
                </tr>
              </tbody>
            </table>
            <div class="code-block" aria-label="Code snippet: attention mechanism implementation">
              <pre><span class="code-kw">def</span> <span class="code-fn">attention</span><span class="code-punc">(</span><span class="code-var">self</span><span class="code-punc">,</span> Q<span class="code-punc">,</span> K<span class="code-punc">,</span> V<span class="code-punc">):</span>
    <span class="code-var">d_k</span> <span class="code-op">=</span> Q<span class="code-punc">.</span>shape<span class="code-punc">[-</span><span class="code-num">1</span><span class="code-punc">]</span>
    <span class="code-var">scores</span> <span class="code-op">=</span> <span class="code-punc">(</span>Q <span class="code-op">@</span> K<span class="code-punc">.</span><span class="code-fn">transpose</span><span class="code-punc">(-</span><span class="code-num">2</span><span class="code-punc">, -</span><span class="code-num">1</span><span class="code-punc">))</span> <span class="code-op">/</span> math<span class="code-punc">.</span><span class="code-fn">sqrt</span><span class="code-punc">(</span>d_k<span class="code-punc">)</span>
    <span class="code-var">weights</span> <span class="code-op">=</span> F<span class="code-punc">.</span><span class="code-fn">softmax</span><span class="code-punc">(</span>scores<span class="code-punc">,</span> dim<span class="code-op">=-</span><span class="code-num">1</span><span class="code-punc">)</span>
    <span class="code-kw">return</span> weights <span class="code-op">@</span> V<span class="code-punc">,</span> weights</pre>
            </div>
            <a
              href="https://github.com/parvpatodia/vit-from-scratch"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener noreferrer"
              class="card-link"
              aria-label="View ViT project on GitHub (opens in new tab)"
            >
              <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M9 19c-5 1.5-5-2.5-7-3m14 6v-3.87a3.37 3.37 0 0 0-.94-2.61c3.14-.35 6.44-1.54 6.44-7A5.44 5.44 0 0 0 20 4.77 5.07 5.07 0 0 0 19.91 1S18.73.65 16 2.48a13.38 13.38 0 0 0-7 0C6.27.65 5.09 1 5.09 1A5.07 5.07 0 0 0 5 4.77a5.44 5.44 0 0 0-1.5 3.78c0 5.42 3.3 6.61 6.44 7A3.37 3.37 0 0 0 9 18.13V22"/></svg>
              View on GitHub
            </a>
          </article>

          <!-- av-policy-lab -->
          <article class="project-card coming-soon fade-in tilt-card" aria-label="AV Policy Lab project, in progress">
            <span class="coming-soon-badge" aria-label="Coming soon">Coming Soon</span>
            <div class="card-header">
              <h4 class="card-title" style="padding-right:7rem;">av-policy-lab</h4>
              <span class="status-badge status-progress">In Progress</span>
            </div>
            <p class="card-period">Summer 2026</p>
            <div class="stack-tags">
              <span class="stack-tag">nuPlan</span>
              <span class="stack-tag">CARLA</span>
              <span class="stack-tag">PyTorch</span>
              <span class="stack-tag">Behavior Cloning</span>
              <span class="stack-tag">Imitation Learning</span>
            </div>
            <p class="card-description">Closed-loop driving policy research comparing three baselines in simulation: pure behavior cloning, MILE-style world-model imitation, and a VLA-flavored policy with language conditioning. Training on nuPlan or CARLA Leaderboard 2.0. The focus is clean baseline execution, honest failure-mode analysis, and a reusable evaluation harness.</p>
            <a
